Chapter: RvBigLiteral
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Every literal above `#7FFFFFFF7FFFFFFF` used to FAULT the riscv plug rather
 than compile, because `rv-li-fits-32` asked whether a value fits in 32 bits by
 adding `#80000000` to the value first, and the addition left the signed 64-bit
 range. The rows below straddle the old boundary by one, so a run of the arm
 places the failure at a byte rather than in a band, and the arm answers the
 second question too: an immediate that now compiles has to come back out of
 the register with every bit intact.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("at-boundary want 9223372034707292159 got " & show #7FFFFFFF7FFFFFFF)
    print-line-uni ("past-boundary want 9223372034707292160 got " & show #7FFFFFFF80000000)
    print-line-uni ("max want 9223372036854775807 got " & show #7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)
    print-line-uni ("max-1 want 9223372036854775806 got " & show #7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFE)
    print-line-uni ("min want -9223372036854775808 got " & show #8000000000000000)
    print-line-uni ("allf want -1 got " & show #FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)
    print-line-uni ("just-over-32 want 2147483648 got " & show 2147483648)
    print-line-uni ("top-of-32 want 2147483647 got " & show 2147483647)
    print-line-uni ("bottom-of-32 want -2147483648 got " & show (0 - 2147483648))
    print-line-uni ("under-32 want -2147483649 got " & show (0 - 2147483649))
  end
